//RS //! Codegen is deliberately dumb (invariant I3): no checking happens here.
//RS //! If a Program reaches this module, emission must always succeed and the
//RS //! resulting Rust must always compile.
//RS //!
//RS //! Type-alignment rules (so emitted Rust always typechecks):
//RS //!   - scalar params (Int/Float/Bool) pass by value, String by `&String`;
//RS //!     `mut` params are `&mut T`; `take` params are `T` by value
//RS //!   - a name bound to a `&T`/`&mut T` parameter is always emitted as the
//RS //!     place `(*__jet_x)`, so every name has its plain Jet type
//RS //!   - every printed/interpolated value goes through the `JetShow` trait
//RS //!     in the prelude (Float keeps its decimal part there, S21)
//RS //!   - every operator result is fully parenthesized
