//RS /// Emitted at the top of every program: core runtime helpers used by generated Rust.
//RS /// Parts stay in source order so splitting ownership never changes generated bytes.
//RS ///
//RS /// Every part here is spliced flat into the generated crate root, so one
//RS /// namespace holds all of them: item names must be unique across parts, a part
//RS /// may only use `pub`, `pub(crate)`, or private visibility (`pub(super)` has
//RS /// no parent at the root), and Foundation items are named unqualified or
//RS /// through the `jet_foundation` facade (`push_foundation_facade`).
//RS ///
//RS /// `Outcome.rs` is not listed: it is the `outcome` root of
//RS /// `EMBEDDED_PRELUDE_PARTS`, whose dependency closure (JSON kernel,
//RS /// `RuntimeDiagnosticCore`) `push_cached_runtime_body` emits before these.
