//RS     // parser, error vocabulary, and the diagnostic renderer it imports as
//RS     // `crate::RuntimeDiagnosticCore` all live in the same cached rlib instead
//RS     // of the optional Core closure, which is a separate crate when native
//RS     // runtime reuse is active.  Data-loader and Arrow C-data sources are
//RS     // demand-driven Core dependencies; keeping them here would make a print-only
//RS     // program carry their code and unsafe FFI surface.
