//RS /// Evaluate one generated contract case's pre-call eligibility (D-CLAIM1,
//RS /// #2502). The compiler-synthesized predicate checks the candidate's own
//RS /// `#Pre` conditions over the generated arguments BEFORE the callable runs:
//RS /// `Ok(false)` is a rejected input and the callable never executes. Once the
//RS /// predicate accepts, the callable runs under ordinary `jet_test_run`
//RS /// semantics — its own `#Pre`/`#Post` and every nested callee failure are
//RS /// real failure evidence, never reclassified as input rejection. The lowered
//RS /// predicate carries its checked `JetOutcome<bool, JetErr>` result; a returned
//RS /// `JetErr` is failure evidence too. A panic while evaluating the predicate
//RS /// itself is failure evidence as well: the sampler found an input on which the
//RS /// precondition cannot even be evaluated.
